    { math: '1 · Repetition is structure', note: 'Music marks its sections by returning: A–A (hymn), A–B (through-composed = no return), A–B–A (return home). Memory needs landmarks; form plants them.' },
    { math: '2 · Binary and ternary', note: 'Binary (A–B): two balanced halves, the dance-music norm. Ternary (A–B–A): departure and return — the oldest satisfaction in music, from baroque dances to pop choruses.' },
